** Atomic data from version 10.1 of the CHIANTI database **
%File prepared for the CHIANTI atomic database by Peter Young.
%File:  cr_2.elvlc
%Theoretical energies:
    Tayal S.S., Zatsarinny O., 2020, ApJ, 888, 10
%Observed energies:
    Kramida, A., Ralchenko, Yu., Reader, J., and NIST ASD Team (2019).
    NIST Atomic Spectra Database (ver. 5.7.1), [Online].
    Available: https://physics.nist.gov/asd [2020, July 23].
    National Institute of Standards and Technology, Gaithersburg, MD.
    DOI: https://doi.org/10.18434/T4W30F
%Comment:
    I assigned observed energies automatically by cross-matching configuration, term, J-value
    and energy with the Tayal data. Note that theoretical energies are in very good agreement
    with the NIST energies. Labels for the levels come from NIST.
%filename: cr_2.wgfa
%File prepared for the CHIANTI atomic database by Peter Young.
%File:  cr_2.wgfa
%A-values:
    Tayal S.S., Zatsarinny O., 2020, ApJ, 888, 10
%gf-values:
    Tayal S.S., Zatsarinny O., 2020, ApJ, 888, 10
%Wavelengths:
    Derived from energies in elvlc file.
%File processed with wgfa_tidy by pryoung on 23-Jul-2020
%filename: cr_2.scups
%File:  cr_2.scups
%File prepared for the CHIANTI atomic database by Peter Young.
%Upsilons:
    Tayal S.S., Zatsarinny O., 2020, ApJ, 888, 10
%gf-values:
    Tayal S.S., Zatsarinny O., 2020, ApJ, 888, 10 [taken from wgfa file]
%Theoretical energies:
    Tayal S.S., Zatsarinny O., 2020, ApJ, 888, 10
%Comment:
    I removed transitions for which the lower level was not a metastable level. There are 117
    metastable levels (including ground).
    Tayal & Zatsarinny stated that their upsilons were computed from 10^2 to 10^5 K, but their
    data file only covers 10^3 to 10^5 K.
    Of the 50322 transitions, most were fit automatically with write_scups.pro. The remaining
    513 transitions were fit by hand with write_scups_gui. No problems with the data were found.
